     1	/**
     2	 * Theme composition regression tests.
     3	 *
     4	 * The design foundations are token data, not logic, so most of them can't break
     5	 * in an interesting way. Two things genuinely can, and neither surfaces as a
     6	 * build or type error:
     7	 *
     8	 *   1. A foundation stops reaching the composed theme (a missing key in
     9	 *      `theme/index.ts`, or `extendTheme` clobbering a base scale).
    10	 *   2. Someone remaps a Chakra scale key onto the Zimmermann value of the same
    11	 *      name. Four of the five design-system font sizes collide with Chakra
    12	 *      defaults (`md`, `xs`, `2xs`, `3xs`), and the base retail-react-app uses
    13	 *      those names at ~199 call sites — so remapping silently restyles base
    14	 *      components. See the `scale token collisions` block below.
